menu "Satura Bridge"

choice SATURA_BOARD
    prompt "Hardware board"
    default SATURA_BOARD_GENERIC
    help
        Selects which main/board/board_*.c backend is compiled into
        the build. Application code (WiFi, BT PAN, NAT, HTTP, DNS,
        clipboard, device name, ...) does not change based on this
        choice — only main/board/ does. Exactly one backend is ever
        compiled in.

    config SATURA_BOARD_GENERIC
        bool "Generic ESP32 DevKit"
        help
            No PMIC, no battery. board_get_battery_percent() and
            related calls always report "unavailable".

    config SATURA_BOARD_CORE2
        bool "M5Stack Core2 (original, AXP192)"
        help
            Not the Core2 v1.1 revision — that one uses an AXP2101
            PMIC instead, which this backend does not support.

    config SATURA_BOARD_STICKC_PLUS2
        bool "M5StickC Plus2"
        help
            No PMIC on this board. Power hold is done via GPIO4 and
            battery voltage via ADC on GPIO38. Charging status is not
            available on this board (no documented signal for it).

endchoice

endmenu
